"A careful answer."
"You would distrust an unlimited one."
{n}Her thumb moves once against your cheek. Then she takes her hand away and leans back, and lets you want the next one, because she enjoys watching it.
The pear has begun to brown on its cut surface. Neither of you improves it.{/n}

{n}She leaves the place beside her open and moves the plate to it. You take the chair near the window.
